PRIVACY = dict(
    answer="AL Elite Financing is a matching service, not a lender. When you submit a request, we use the information you give us to match you with lenders or financing programs and, with your permission, share it with them so they can contact you. We do not sell your personal information for money. This policy explains what we collect, how we use and share it, how long we keep it, and the choices and rights you have.",
    prose=f"""<p><em>Effective {EFFECTIVE}.</em></p>
<h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2><p>AL Elite Financing ("AL Elite", "we", "us") operates alelitefinancing.com, a marketplace that matches homeowners with consumer lenders for home improvement projects and contractors with customer-financing programs and business lenders. We are not a lender, bank or credit union. We do not make credit decisions, set rates or fund loans. Lenders in our network make their own decisions under their own privacy policies. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a> or {PHONE}.</p>
<h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
<h3>Information you give us</h3><ul><li><strong>Request forms:</strong> name, email, phone, state, the type of project or business need, approximate amount, whether insurance is involved, timing, and anything you type in a message field.</li><li><strong>Download forms:</strong> name, email and phone when you request a worksheet or guide.</li><li><strong>Contractor applications:</strong> company name, trade, licensing and insurance details, and contact information.</li><li><strong>Correspondence:</strong> emails, calls and messages you send us.</li></ul>
<p>We do not ask for, and you should not send us, Social Security numbers, bank account or card numbers, government ID numbers or full credit reports. Those are collected by a lender, if at all, on the lender's own application.</p>
<h3>Information collected automatically</h3><ul><li><strong>Usage data:</strong> pages viewed, links clicked, calculator inputs you enter on the page (processed in your browser and not sent to us unless you submit a form), referring site, approximate location from your IP address, device and browser type.</li><li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> we use strictly necessary cookies to run the site and may use analytics cookies to understand how it's used. See "Cookies" below.</li></ul>
<h3>Information from others</h3><p>Lenders and partners may tell us whether a request resulted in contact or a funded loan so we can measure the service and be paid. We may receive business information about contractors from licensing boards and public records.</p>
<h2 id="how-we-use">How we use it</h2><ul><li>To match your request with lenders, financing programs or partner contractors that serve your state and project type.</li><li>To send the resource you requested and related guides, and to respond to you.</li><li>To contact you about your request by email, phone or text, where you have agreed to that on the form.</li><li>To operate, secure and improve the site, including measuring which pages and tools people use.</li><li>To comply with law, enforce our terms and protect against fraud and abuse.</li></ul>
<h2 id="sharing">When and with whom we share it</h2><ul><li><strong>Lenders and financing programs:</strong> when you submit a request, we share the information you gave us with one or more lenders or programs in our network that serve your state and project so they can contact you with options. Once shared, their privacy policies govern their use. You can ask us which lenders received your information.</li><li><strong>Partner contractors:</strong> if you ask to be connected with a contractor, or a contractor's customer uses our financing tools, we share the information needed for that purpose.</li><li><strong>Service providers:</strong> companies that host the site, deliver email, process forms and provide analytics, under contracts that limit their use of your data to our instructions.</li><li><strong>Legal and safety:</strong> when required by law, court order or to protect rights, safety and property.</li><li><strong>Business transfers:</strong> if AL Elite is sold or merged, your information may transfer with it under this policy.</li></ul>
<p>We are paid by lenders and programs for introductions. Under some state privacy laws, sharing personal information in exchange for payment can be treated as a "sale" or "sharing" even though we do not sell data to data brokers. You can opt out at any time; see <a href="/do-not-sell/">Do not sell or share my information</a>.</p>
<h2 id="consent">Calls, texts and email</h2><p>When you submit a request and agree to be contacted, you authorise AL Elite and the lenders or partners we match you with to contact you at the number and email you provided, including by automated dialing, prerecorded messages and text messages where permitted by law, even if your number is on a Do Not Call list. Consent is not a condition of purchase. Reply STOP to any text to stop texts, click unsubscribe in any email, or contact us to update your preferences. Message and data rates may apply.</p>
<h2 id="cookies">Cookies and analytics</h2><p>Strictly necessary cookies keep the site working. Analytics cookies, where used, help us see which pages and tools are useful; they do not identify you by name. Your browser can block or delete cookies; the site will still work, though some features may not remember your preferences. We honour Global Privacy Control signals where required by law.</p>
<h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2><p>We keep request and correspondence records for as long as needed to provide the service, meet legal and accounting obligations and resolve disputes, typically up to five years after your last interaction, then delete or de-identify them. Download-form records are kept while you remain subscribed to related emails and for a reasonable period afterwards.</p>
<h2 id="security">Security</h2><p>We use encrypted connections (HTTPS) for the site and forms, limit access to personal information to people who need it, and use reputable providers for hosting and email. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
<h2 id="rights">Your choices and rights</h2><p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to know what personal information we hold about you, to receive a copy, to correct or delete it, to opt out of its sale or sharing, to limit use of sensitive information, and not to be discriminated against for exercising these rights. Residents of California, Colorado, Connecticut, Texas, Virginia, Utah, Oregon, Montana and other states with general privacy laws can exercise these rights by emailing <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a> with the subject "Privacy request", calling {PHONE}, or using the <a href="/do-not-sell/">opt-out page</a>. We will verify your identity by matching the details you provide with our records, respond within the time the applicable law allows (generally 45 days), and will not charge a fee for reasonable requests. An authorised agent may submit a request on your behalf with written permission. If we deny a request you may appeal by replying to our response.</p>
<h2 id="children">Children</h2><p>The site is for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18. If you believe a minor has submitted information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>
<h2 id="third-parties">Links and third parties</h2><p>Our pages link to lenders, government sites and other resources. Their privacy practices are their own. Our financing calculators run in your browser and do not send your inputs to us.</p>
<h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2><p>We will post changes here with a new effective date. Material changes will be flagged on this page, and where required we will notify you by email.</p>
<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2><p>AL Elite Financing · <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a> · {PHONE}. Registered business address available on request.</p>""")

TERMS = dict(
    answer="These terms govern your use of alelitefinancing.com and our matching service. The short version: we are a marketplace, not a lender; we match your request with lenders and programs who make their own decisions; we don't guarantee an offer, a rate or an approval; the calculators and guides are general information, not advice; and by submitting a request you agree to be contacted as described in our privacy policy.",
    prose=f"""<p><em>Effective {EFFECTIVE}.</em> By using this site or submitting a request you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>
<h2 id="service">1. What the service is</h2><p>AL Elite Financing ("AL Elite", "we") operates a lead-matching marketplace. Homeowners tell us about a project; contractors tell us about a business need or a wish to offer customer financing. We match those requests with lenders, financing programs and partner contractors in our network that serve the relevant state and project type, and share the request with them so they can respond. We are not a lender, bank, credit union, broker or financial adviser. We do not make credit decisions, set rates or fund loans. Any loan, program or contractor agreement is solely between you and that third party under their terms.</p>
<h2 id="no-guarantee">2. No guarantee of offers, rates or approval</h2><p>Submitting a request is free and is not a loan application. We do not guarantee that any lender will contact you, make an offer, approve you or offer any particular rate, term or amount. Payment figures, cost ranges and examples on this site are illustrations based on standard amortization and typical national ranges; they are not quotes or offers of credit. Lender availability and products vary by state.</p>
<h2 id="your-information">3. Information you provide</h2><p>You agree that the information you submit is accurate and that you are at least 18 and authorised to provide it. Do not submit Social Security numbers, bank or card numbers or other sensitive identifiers; lenders will collect what they need on their own applications. You are responsible for keeping copies of anything you submit.</p>
<h2 id="contact-consent">4. Consent to be contacted</h2><p>When you submit a request and agree to be contacted, you authorise AL Elite and the lenders, programs and partners we match you with to contact you at the number and email you provided, including by automated dialing, prerecorded messages and texts where permitted by law, even if your number is on a Do Not Call list. Consent is not a condition of purchase; you may withdraw it at any time by replying STOP to a text, unsubscribing from an email or contacting us. Message and data rates may apply.</p>
<h2 id="compensation">5. How we are paid</h2><p>Lenders and financing programs pay us for introductions, and partner contractors pay for program services. Compensation does not affect the rate or decision a lender gives you, which the lender sets independently, and we do not accept payment to steer you to a worse offer. See <a href="/how-we-make-money/">how we make money</a>.</p>
<h2 id="contractors">6. Contractors and partner programs</h2><p>Contractors who join a partner program must hold the licences and insurance required where they work, present financing truthfully, never promise approval or quote rates not provided in writing by the lender, and never offer to waive, absorb or rebate an insurance deductible. We may remove a contractor from a program at our discretion. Program terms, fees and funding schedules are set out in the program agreement, which controls over these terms if they conflict.</p>
<h2 id="tools-content">7. Calculators, guides and content</h2><p>Our calculators run in your browser using the numbers you enter and standard formulas; results depend on your inputs and are estimates. Guides, cost ranges and local pages are general information drawn from public sources and industry practice; they are not legal, tax, insurance or financial advice and may not reflect your situation or current law. Get itemised quotes from licensed contractors, read your insurance policy, and consult a professional where it matters.</p>
<h2 id="acceptable-use">8. Acceptable use</h2><p>You agree not to submit false or third-party information without authority, scrape or copy the site at scale, interfere with its operation, use it to send spam, or use it for any unlawful purpose. We may block access for misuse.</p>
<h2 id="ip">9. Intellectual property</h2><p>The site, its text, tools, worksheets and images are owned by AL Elite or its licensors. You may use them for personal, non-commercial purposes and may print or download our worksheets for your own use. Lender and manufacturer names and marks belong to their owners and are used for identification only.</p>
<h2 id="third-party">10. Third-party sites and services</h2><p>Links to lenders, government agencies and other sites are provided for convenience. We don't control them and aren't responsible for their content, accuracy or practices.</p>
<h2 id="disclaimer">11. Disclaimer of warranties</h2><p>The site and service are provided "as is" and "as available". To the fullest extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy and non-infringement, and we do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted or error-free.</p>
<h2 id="liability">12. Limitation of liability</h2><p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, AL Elite and its owners, employees and partners are not liable for indirect, incidental, consequential, special or punitive damages, or for any loss arising from a lender's, program's or contractor's acts, decisions, products or services, or from your reliance on content or calculator results. Our total liability for any claim relating to the site or service is limited to $100. Some states do not allow certain limitations, so some of these may not apply to you.</p>
<h2 id="indemnity">13. Indemnity</h2><p>You agree to indemnify AL Elite against claims arising from your breach of these terms or your misuse of the site.</p>
<h2 id="disputes">14. Disputes and governing law</h2><p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas, without regard to conflict-of-law rules, and any dispute will be brought in the state or federal courts located in Texas, unless applicable law gives you the right to proceed elsewhere. Before filing any claim, you agree to contact us at <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a> so we can try to resolve it informally within 30 days.</p>
<h2 id="changes">15. Changes</h2><p>We may update these terms by posting a new version with a new effective date. Continued use after the change means you accept it.</p>
<h2 id="contact">16. Contact</h2><p>AL Elite Financing · <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a> · {PHONE}.</p>""")

ACCESS = dict(
    answer="AL Elite Financing wants everyone to be able to use this site, including people who use screen readers, keyboard navigation, magnification or reduced-motion settings. We build to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at Level AA, test as we publish, and fix problems when they are reported. If something on the site doesn't work for you, tell us and we will provide the information another way while we fix it.",
    prose=f"""<p><em>Last reviewed {EFFECTIVE}.</em></p>
<h2 id="standard">The standard we work to</h2><p>Our target is <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/" rel="noopener">WCAG 2.2 Level AA</a>. We treat it as a working standard rather than a one-time certificate: every new page, tool and form is checked against it before publishing, and we re-check the site periodically.</p>
<h2 id="measures">What we've done</h2><ul><li><strong>Semantic structure:</strong> one H1 per page, headings in order, landmarks (header, navigation, main, footer), lists and tables marked up as such, and breadcrumbs on every page.</li><li><strong>Keyboard access:</strong> every link, button, form field, calculator control and the mobile menu can be reached and used with a keyboard, with a visible focus indicator. The Calculators menu opens on focus as well as hover.</li><li><strong>Colour and contrast:</strong> body text and links meet the 4.5:1 contrast ratio; links are blue and underlined so they don't rely on colour alone; the site renders in both light and dark system settings.</li><li><strong>Forms:</strong> every field has a visible label, required fields are marked, errors are described in text, and submission results are announced to assistive technology.</li><li><strong>Calculators:</strong> inputs are labelled, results are in live regions that screen readers announce when values change, and nothing requires a mouse.</li><li><strong>Images:</strong> informative images have descriptive alt text; decorative ones are hidden from assistive technology. Our local snapshot cards repeat their key facts in the page text.</li><li><strong>Motion and zoom:</strong> no auto-playing media; the site respects reduced-motion settings; text can be resized to 200% and the layout reflows on narrow screens without horizontal scrolling.</li><li><strong>Downloads:</strong> our PDF worksheets are tagged, fillable and have a reading order; we also provide their key content on the related web page.</li></ul>
<h2 id="limits">Known limitations</h2><ul><li>The embedded Google Map on our location band is provided by Google and may not be fully operable by keyboard; the same locations are listed as text links beside it.</li><li>Some older PDF worksheets may have incomplete tagging; we are updating them and will provide any content in an accessible format on request.</li><li>Third-party lender and government sites we link to have their own accessibility practices.</li></ul>
<h2 id="feedback">Tell us about a problem</h2><p>If you have trouble using any part of this site, email <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a> with "Accessibility" in the subject or call {PHONE}. Tell us the page, what you were trying to do and the assistive technology you use. We aim to respond within two business days and to provide the information you need by phone or email while we fix the issue.</p>
<h2 id="compatibility">Technical details</h2><p>The site is built with standard HTML, CSS and a small amount of JavaScript, and is designed to work with current versions of Chrome, Safari, Firefox and Edge, and with screen readers including VoiceOver, NVDA and JAWS. Calculators require JavaScript; the explanatory content on each tool page is available without it.</p>""")

